cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "summit: open-source web security testing platform"
message: >-
  If you use summit in your research or in a paper, please cite the
  project repository.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: pennacle-security
    name: Pennacle Security
    website: "https://github.com/pennacle-security"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pennacle-security/summit"
url: "https://github.com/pennacle-security/summit"
abstract: >-
  summit is a scriptable command-line platform for authorized web security
  testing: an intercepting HTTP proxy, a crawler-driven scanner with
  confidence-labelled findings, a directory fuzzer, WAF fingerprinting and
  bypass probing, broken-link hijack detection, resource takeover
  fingerprints, and recon orchestration for subfinder, httpx and nmap.
keywords:
  - web-security
  - scanner
  - pentest
  - proxy
  - fuzzer
license: MIT
version: v2.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-25"
